    "lawCode": "Amd §142, Ec Dev L",
    "lawSection": "Economic Development Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6397\n\nSPONSOR: KAPLAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the economic development law, in relation to the\npublishing of certain procurement contract opportunities; and providing\nfor the repeal of such provisions upon the expiration thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis legislation would shorten the timeframe to at least five days that\nthe notice of procurement opportunities must be made available as it\nrelates to the COVID-19 pandemic small business recovery grant program.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends Section 142 of the economic development law by adding a\nnew Section 1-a which would notwithstand other provisions of law related\nto procurement contract opportunities that are required to effectuate\nthe COVID-19 pandemic small business recovery program (Section sixteen-\nff of section one of the Urban Development Corporation Act) to allow for\nthe notice to be available for at least five days on the internet.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation seeks to set a five day timeframe for procurement\nreview as it relates to the COVID-19 pandemic small business recovery\ngrant program. Current law requires a fifteen business day timeframe\nthat will slow down the process of getting this critical program up and\nrunning as quickly as possible. Due to the technical and detailed nature\nof the act, the number of contractors that could undertake such a\nproject are limited, and it is incredibly likely that those who are\ninterested in procuring this contract are anticipating their bid, are\nready to bid, and do not need a longer timeframe to organize their bid.\nThis narrowly limited bill takes into account the very real circum-\nstances that every day small businesses do not have access to this\nmoney, their likelihood of going out of business increases. In order to\nsave our small businesses this truncated timeframe is justified and\nnecessary to get assistance out the door as quickly as possible for this\nspecific program.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately and shall expire and be deemed\nrepealed on July 31, 2021.\n",
